ry — no way to define field-specific filter criteria or view only matching entries.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With no field sort active, dragged \\\"Design new landing page\\\" via keyboard (Space/Arrow/Space) to a new position in Table view (result: Review, Update, Design, Prepare, Team, Test Entry Alpha) and separately in Card view (result: Review, Update, Prepare, Team, Design, Test Entry Alpha). Switching between views preserved each view's distinct manual order; entry count (6) and values unaffected.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No data import feature exists in the application\", \"actual\": \"Searched the Configure Fields dialog (which references importing data in a note), the main toolbar, and the full DOM (no input[type=file], no button/link/menuitem containing \\\"import\\\") — there is no UI control to import data at all, so field-schema-gated import validation cannot be exercised.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In Add Entry form, typing \\\"abc\\\" into the Priority number field left it unchanged at \\\"0\\\" (non-numeric characters rejected by the numeric input). Typing \\\"42\\\" was accepted and, after submission, the entry displayed \\\"42\\\" correctly in the Priority column.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Attempting to set the Due Date field to an invalid calendar date \\\"2026-13-45\\\" (month 13, day 45) resulted in the date input being cleared/rejected (value reverted to empty) rather than accepting the invalid date, confirming the date field enforces valid calendar dates only.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After sorting by Priority (asc/desc) and Due Date (asc), entry count remained \\\"6 entries\\\" throughout and each entry's field values (Task Name, Priority, Due Date, Completed, Notes) were unchanged, only order changed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No filter feature exists to verify inclusion/exclusion criteria or restoration behavior\", \"actual\": \"No filter UI could be located anywhere in the app (toolbar, headers, dialogs, or DOM scan for \\\"filter\\\"-related attributes), so field-specific filter criteria cannot be applied or cleared.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 6 entries and every field (Task Name, Priority, Due Date, Completed, Notes) shown consistently in both table and card views; empty Notes value rendered as \\\"—\\\" placeholder in both views.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Configure Fields dialog shows labeled type dropdowns (Text/Number/Date/Checkbox) per field; Add Entry form renders type-appropriate controls: textbox for text, spinbutton for number, native input[type=date] for date, checkbox toggle (No/Yes) for checkbox.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Form checkbox toggles between \\\"Completed No\\\" and \\\"Completed Yes\\\" [checked] state. Table view renders green check icon (text-success) for true vs gray X icon (text-muted-foreground) for false.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Quick search does not match displayed/formatted field values for date and checkbox fields\", \"actual\": \"Searching \\\"Jan 15\\\" (the exact due-date text shown for \\\"Design new landing page\\\") returned \\\"0 entries matching \\\\\\\"Jan 15\\\\\\\"\\\" instead of matching that entry. Searching \\\"Yes\\\" (the exact Completed value shown for several entries) also returned 0 results. Search appears to only match raw/internal values (e.g. ISO date strings or text/number fields), not the human-readable values rendered in the UI.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing \\\"test\\\" (lowercase) matched \\\"Test Entry Alpha\\\" (capitalized) — case-insensitive text match; footer showed \\\"1 entry matching \\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\"\\\". Clearing the search restored all 6 entries in prior order.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Selecting \\\"Priority\\\" in Sort menu immediately reordered cards; Sort button label changed to \\\"Priority\\\" and footer showed \\\"Sorted by Priority (ascending)\\\"/\\\"(descending)\\\" after toggling. App remained fully interactive after sorting (view switch, further clicks worked).\"}]}"
